{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1025","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1025","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1025\",\"parent_revision\":\"63e4cbf037031999b2111df665dac6af9e223103\",\"root_revision\":\"3bce9bb4a96fad07bed3160fa4179c0107d36d825ed051dbf6e7878ce1b6c49b\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nP1015 introduced 38 tests in test_backend_status.py using `unittest.mock`. Project standard requires pytest-mock for all new tests. The tests are functionally correct but inconsistent with the established pattern. Replace all `MagicMock`/`patch` usages with `mocker.MagicMock()`/`mocker.patch()` and remove unused `monkeypatch` parameters.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-24T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-24T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **refactor: replace unittest.mock with pytest-mock in test_backend_status.py** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Not specified\\n- **Priority**: P3\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-23\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-03-30)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n7/10 \u2014 Consistency refactor with no functional change. pytest-mock is the project standard; this file is the only outlier. Inconsistency increases cognitive load and raises questions in code review about whether the divergence is intentional.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Bottleneck: Any reviewer seeing `unittest.mock` in this file must check whether it is intentional divergence or oversight.\\n- Blocks: Nothing is blocked, but the inconsistency is visible in code review and static analysis.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Brings `test_backend_status.py` into full alignment with the project-wide pytest-mock standard.\\n- Allows future refactors (e.g., mocker fixture auto-cleanup, spy/AsyncMock helpers) to apply uniformly across all tests.\\n- Removes the `from unittest.mock import MagicMock, patch` import line, reducing stdlib dependencies in the test file.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nAfter the refactor:\\n- `test_backend_status.py` contains no `from unittest.mock import ...` statement.\\n- `_make_dh_paths_mock` accepts a `mocker` parameter or is replaced inline with `mocker.MagicMock()`.\\n- All `with patch(...)` context managers are replaced with `mocker.patch(...)` calls.\\n- `monkeypatch` parameters remain where used for `setenv`/`delenv`/`setattr`; they are only removed from signatures where the parameter is declared but never called.\\n- `conftest.py` mock_github fixture replaces `from unittest.mock import MagicMock` with `mocker` injection or removes the import if MagicMock is sourced from `pytest_mock`.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `grep -n 'from unittest.mock\\\\|unittest\\\\.mock' plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backend_status.py` returns no matches.\\n2. `grep -n 'from unittest.mock\\\\|unittest\\\\.mock' plugins/development-harness/tests/conftest.py` returns no matches (if conftest MagicMock usages are migrated).\\n3. `grep -rn 'with patch(' plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backend_status.py` returns no matches (all replaced with mocker.patch).\\n4. `cd plugins/development-harness && uv run pytest tests/test_backend_status.py -q` exits 0 with 38 tests passing.\\n5. `cd plugins/development-harness && uv run pytest tests/ -q` exits 0 (full test suite still passes).\\n6. `cd plugins/development-harness && uv run ruff check tests/test_backend_status.py` exits 0.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/tests/test_agent_profile/test_server.py \u2014 canonical mocker.patch() usage |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/test_groom_mark_groomed.py \u2014 canonical mocker.patch() and mocker.MagicMock() usage |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/tests/conftest.py \u2014 also imports unittest.mock.MagicMock, in scope for this refactor |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/pyproject.toml \u2014 confirms pytest-mock>=3.15.1 is already a declared dependency |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 pytest-mock is already installed.\\n- Blocks: None \u2014 purely internal consistency change.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 ~140 lines of mechanical substitution across one file (plus minor conftest.py cleanup). No logic changes. The only judgment call is deciding whether `_make_dh_paths_mock` should become a fixture or receive `mocker` as a parameter \u2014 either works, but converting it to a fixture accepting `mocker` is the standard pytest-mock pattern.\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- None. pytest-mock is declared in pyproject.toml and confirmed in uv.lock. The reference pattern is established in at least two other test files in the same plugin.\\n\\n### Output / Evidence\\n\\n- `grep` output from step 1\u20134 above confirms the 4 locations of `unittest.mock` usage.\\n- File: `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backend_status.py` line 18 (import), line 329\u2013340 (`_make_dh_paths_mock` standalone helper), and ~10 test methods using `with patch()`.\\n- File: `plugins/development-harness/tests/conftest.py` line 17 (import) and lines 84, 85, 101 (`MagicMock` usage in `mock_github` fixture).\\n- Note: `monkeypatch` in this file is NOT unused \u2014 it is actively used for `setenv`, `delenv`, and `setattr`. Only the `monkeypatch` parameter in integration tests (TestBacklogListBackendIntegration) that declare it but make no `monkeypatch.*` calls should be removed.\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n1. Run `grep -n 'from unittest.mock' plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backend_status.py` \u2014 observe line 18: `from unittest.mock import MagicMock, patch`.\\n2. Run `grep -n 'with patch(' plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backend_status.py` \u2014 observe ~10 context manager usages across TestProbeBackendStatusReachable, TestProbeBackendStatusGitHubUnreachable, TestProbeBackendStatusRateLimited, TestProbeBackendStatusCountFetchFailure, TestBacklogListBackendIntegration.\\n3. Run `grep -n 'MagicMock()' plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backend_status.py` \u2014 observe usages in `_make_dh_paths_mock` (line 338) and test methods (lines 405\u2013408, 425\u2013428, 445\u2013448, 522, 555, 573, 591).\\n4. Run `grep -n 'from unittest.mock' plugins/development-harness/tests/conftest.py` \u2014 observe line 17: `from unittest.mock import MagicMock`.\\n\\n## Artifact Manifest\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n<!-- artifact-manifest:begin -->\\n| Type | Path | Status | Agent | Created |\\n|------|------|--------|-------|---------|\\n| task-plan | /home/ubuntulinuxqa2/.dh/projects/-home-ubuntulinuxqa2-repos-claude_skills/plan/P1023-backlog-list-github-availability-followup-1.yaml | current |  | 2026-03-23T23:51:43Z |\\n| task-plan | plan/P1023-backlog-list-github-availability-followup-1.yaml | current | dh_migrate | 2026-03-24T16:35:27Z |\\n<!-- artifact-manifest:end -->\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"f8399e451696a5101b5c968813b131b630e6ea2b19e16c1ea13233e14fb87f07\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPg7BCg\"}"}